## Context

PR #81 fixed per-command usage strings (user-visible stderr) but the Go
doc-comments above cmdClose, cmdLog, and cmdNew still use `<arg>` angle
brackets. These are not user-visible but are inconsistent with the UPPER_CASE
convention adopted for user-facing strings (PRs #78, #81). Found during /verify
of PR #81.

## Actions

1. `close.go`: update the comment block above `cmdClose` — replace `<id|file>`,
   `<reason>`, `[dir]` with `ID|FILE`, `REASON`, `[DIR]`.
2. `log.go`: update the comment block above `cmdLog` — replace `<id>`, `<line>`,
   `[dir]` with `ID`, `LINE`, `[DIR]`.
3. `new.go`: update the comment block above `cmdNew` — replace `<title>`, `[dir]`
   with `TITLE`, `[DIR]`.

## Test

No test needed — doc-comments are not user-visible and not grep-ratcheted.
Verify manually: `grep -n '[<>]' tickets/tools/go/close.go tickets/tools/go/log.go tickets/tools/go/new.go`
should return no matches after the fix.

## Exit criteria

- `grep -n '[<>]' tickets/tools/go/close.go tickets/tools/go/log.go tickets/tools/go/new.go` returns no matches.
- `make build` passes.
